.git
.env
.venv
venv
node_modules
dist
__pycache__
*.pyc
db/data
db/postgres.log
*.zip

# Docker patterns are anchored at the context root and have no recursion, so a
# bare `node_modules` above only excludes the top-level one. Without these the
# build uploads backend/, dashboard/ and collector/ dependency trees plus the
# local market data (a whole Postgres cluster) into every image build - the
# "transferring context: 280MB" stall. No Dockerfile copies any of these paths.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
data/
# Test/lint caches. On a locked-down Windows install these can be unreadable by
# the build context walker, which fails the whole image build with "Access is denied".
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
